      "text": "LOOK: Sixty-four-year-old rice farmer Roberto Abanilla of Kabacan town, North Cotabato, harvests the remaining crops from his half-hectare farm on Monday, May 4, after portions of his rice field were affected by flooding caused by heavy rains in the past nights.\n\nAbanilla, who has been farming for 10 years, said he expects to harvest around 92 sacks of cereal grains twice a year, but he cannot say how many as of today. He added that he had also prepared for the possible effects of El Niño. 📸 Ivy Tejano / MB",
